    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 77,
        "text": "Hi, Leo. You look tired. Are you still working on your year-end review?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a5aa63196577b2927856eff221f64e03297c70c833be31a4eb90e46c11f26bcf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 83,
        "sourceEnd": 244,
        "text": "Yes, I am. I have to present my learning strategy for the year. I’ve been studying English for twelve months now, and I want to show what worked and what didn’t.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "43cad689d3b9528782462f9f1b0380cff51a137fab3720095aa4b199c8e3228d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 251,
        "sourceEnd": 296,
        "text": "That sounds useful. What’s your main finding?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "446209b9d80fc4b98ed78c8aa9fb7a350c68f77e61df6c26e558e96308e0c861",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 302,
        "sourceEnd": 694,
        "text": "Well, I started with a very ambitious plan: two hours of study every day. But by March, I was already behind. I realized that consistency matters more than intensity. So I changed to thirty minutes every morning, and that worked much better. It was easier to stick to, and I felt less stressed. The shorter routine also made it easier to fit study into a busy day, so I missed fewer sessions.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0a45291851fe63c6c59924dfc9737dd0a7c27226ee86914cfd3a6f5aeacfadb2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 701,
        "sourceEnd": 734,
        "text": "So you dropped the long sessions?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "90b4f360c23286124ed853a915945ca7504661fed9476bcd46254c4f189e40c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 740,
        "sourceEnd": 1021,
        "text": "Not exactly. I kept one long session on Sundays for writing practice, but the daily short sessions became my core routine. That combination gave me both regular practice and time for deeper work. The Sunday session let me focus on longer texts and review my writing more carefully.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a4efa9f33c8ee61475df4e991ff4b5581d1c469a28548cbf8fb100237c2b4161",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1028,
        "sourceEnd": 1105,
        "text": "Good. What about grammar? You used to make the same mistakes again and again.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "2ec8e0cda29c2fedcc144cf4a8ef7dea8b7705ae9305abdd73ce6e427d511bbf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1111,
        "sourceEnd": 1326,
        "text": "Right. I still do sometimes. For example, I often forget the third-person -s in fast speech. And I sometimes use the present perfect when the past simple is better. But I’ve made a checklist for my exam preparation.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2afa5d40ed1b266d998b7b890b48625f93c4894968e5bbeab8a4471cfa6af7ab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1333,
        "sourceEnd": 1359,
        "text": "A checklist? Tell me more.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "79837f7b0618ec1480a1f22607c42bacba7118219dce09682b7ccf4537aa9391",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1365,
        "sourceEnd": 1826,
        "text": "It’s short—only five points. First, check subject-verb agreement in every sentence. Second, ask: is the time clear? If yes, use past simple. Third, for listening, predict the answer type before you hear it. Fourth, for reading, underline the exact words that match the question. Fifth, leave two minutes to transfer answers. These steps help me avoid careless mistakes. The checklist is quick to use, so I can apply it during practice tests without losing time.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "bf28ddd73f8febae4ef0f7a37d127788ed0fc0bba8a4fe3a2ab1ef3e1a8676c6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1833,
        "sourceEnd": 1897,
        "text": "That’s practical. Did you find any resources especially helpful?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "9b92214fae2f640e2d8e957cf94db04b747215c65371821a0da294506d9f8ade",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1903,
        "sourceEnd": 2219,
        "text": "Yes. I listened to short podcasts every day. They improved my listening and gave me new vocabulary. I also kept a vocabulary notebook, but I only reviewed it once a week. That wasn’t enough. Next year, I’ll review it every other day. Reviewing more often should help me remember new words and use them more actively.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0e8c9f312a6da49cfa4fc4b0562ec9f92223eb83e0377094de34694fc79775d0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2226,
        "sourceEnd": 2246,
        "text": "What about speaking?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a4495f4fa6577ecacb42e4346a76165c04635e63c8f11d5f5e0e464559132df6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2252,
        "sourceEnd": 2542,
        "text": "I joined a weekly conversation group. At first, I was nervous, but now I feel more confident. I still make mistakes, but I can keep the conversation going. The group is supportive, and we practice real-life situations. That regular speaking practice has made a big difference in my fluency.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "b0c43a85318264dfb29e38f283c84d00703638f572235a2435e158d6e451e9a4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2549,
        "sourceEnd": 2583,
        "text": "So what’s your plan for next year?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "063b67755486d49bb6f19693bcbe191040f5eebf4931a77a9ba145a1f7978a73",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2589,
        "sourceEnd": 2923,
        "text": "I want to focus on two things: speaking fluency and reading speed. I’ll continue the daily thirty-minute sessions, but I’ll add a ten-minute review of my mistakes every Friday. And I’ll take a mock test once a month to track my progress. The monthly test will show me whether my reading speed is improving and where I still need work.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "83ceaefdce4f4867f0892d407cc1e67978a3f7e30e9e1725c3e95e8e5564da1b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2930,
        "sourceEnd": 2983,
        "text": "That sounds balanced. Will you change your checklist?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a36130ef168d7eef75de7a7fbca34118e3430312f2860a8b94784bebed1481f2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2989,
        "sourceEnd": 3193,
        "text": "Yes, I’ll update it every month. The checklist should reflect my current errors, not old ones. That way it stays useful. If I notice a new mistake pattern, I can add it and remove points I no longer need.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "9f0d2b65b62db1cc1d93517586189b25a71254331310a9d73b75ad81ba1cbc6a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3200,
        "sourceEnd": 3270,
        "text": "One last question: what advice would you give to someone starting now?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c0006f32bd46d30fc8f26f3c44a41c01306fce0f1fb9a99871a67172b0ad16e1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 3276,
        "sourceEnd": 3471,
        "text": "Start small. Don’t plan two hours a day if you can’t keep it. And review your mistakes regularly—that’s where the real progress is. Also, be patient with yourself; learning a language takes time.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0455c06b9a55c74bd13afa9db0b5e4d3566de9f1e8b03bdb66faefd34b29e95c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
